      {
        "id": "beyond-yield",
        "kind": "transfer",
        "blocks": [],
        "lead": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Yield stress is where the straight, recoverable part of the stress–strain curve ends. The ultimate strength is the highest stress the bar can hold before it necks and breaks."
          }
        ],
        "reveal": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "300 MPa is past the 250 MPa yield stress but below the 400 MPa ultimate strength. Unloading removes only the elastic part of the stretch, so a permanent set remains."
          }
        ],
        "diagram": {
