      "keyIdea": "Stress is force over area, and in the elastic range it is E times the strain. Past yield, a bar keeps a permanent stretch.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "You turned a 20 kN pull on 400 mm² into 50 MPa, and found that it stretches a 2,000 mm steel bar by 0.5 mm."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "The same stress stretches a 1,400 mm aluminium bar by 1 mm, because aluminium is less stiff."
        }
      ],
